 is a surgical procedure related to the patient's cancer treatment.", "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DOCTOR PESSET:", "GASTROSTOMÍA RADIOLOGICA PERCUTÁNEA:Gastrostomía radiológica percutánea es un procedimiento médico que permite la alimentación a través de un tubo insertado en el estómago, utilizado en pacientes con dificultades para tragar.", "AFAGIA:Afagia es la incapacidad para tragar, que puede ser consecuencia de intervenciones quirúrgicas o condiciones médicas.", "SUPLEMENTOS NUTRICIONALES ORALES:Suplementos nutricionales orales son productos diseñados para complementar la dieta y proporcionar nutrientes adicionales, utilizados en pacientes con deficiencias nutricionales.", "CCEE:CCEE, or Consultas Externas Especializadas, refers to specialized medical services that provide care to patients who do not require continuous hospitalization. These services focus on offering specialized follow-up and treatment, ensuring that patients receive the necessary medical attention without the need for an inpatient stay.", "UN:The UN, in this context, refers to a medical unit that plays a crucial role in the nutritional assessment and treatment of patients, especially in complex cases. Additionally, the UN encompasses the nursing unit responsible for the overall care of the patient, which includes daily wound care and dietary recommendations. This dual focus highlights the UN's commitment to providing comprehensive medical support and specialized nursing care to enhance patient outcomes.", "GRP:GRP refers to a prophylactic gastrostomy placement that was requested for the patient, serving as a medical intervention to provide nutritional support. This type of feeding tube is utilized for patients who are unable to take food orally, indicating its importance in ensuring adequate nutrition. The gastrostomy route through which the patient received this nutritional support is critical for their recovery post-surgery, highlighting the essential role of GRP in the patient's overall treatment plan.", "VARÓN DE 66 AÑOS:The patient is a 66-year-old male who has undergone surgery for laryngeal carcinoma and is receiving nutritional support.", "TOMOGRAFÍA COMPUTERIZADA:Tomografía computerizada (CT) is a diagnostic imaging procedure that revealed the extent of the patient's cancer.", "ACÚFENOS:Acúfenos refers to the ringing or buzzing in the ears that the patient experienced, prompting further medical evaluation.", "TOMOGRAFÍA COMPUTERIZADA DE CUELLO:Tomografía computerizada de cuello is a diagnostic imaging procedure that revealed the presence of neoplasia and adenopathies in the patient.", "COMITÉ DE TUMORES:The Comité de Tumores is a medical committee dedicated to evaluating patients' cases to determine appropriate treatment options for cancer. This committee plays a crucial role in assessing cancer diagnoses and formulating treatment plans, ensuring that patients receive tailored and effective care based on their specific medical needs.", "CENTRO DE ESPECIALIDADES:"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}